[2026-02-04T00:21:35.374Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n\n## REQUIREMENT\n\n# Barnes-Hut Tree for O(n log n) Force Layout\n\n## Metadata\n- **Category**: performance\n- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Scan Type**: perf_optimizer\n- **Generated**: 2/1/2026, 11:42:50 PM\n\n## Description\nReplace O(n�) repulsion calculations in graphAlgorithms.ts:753-776 with Barnes-Hut spatial partitioning. Currently, forceLayout runs nested loops over all node pairs for 100 iterations�for 500 nodes this means 25M+ force calculations. A quadtree-based Barnes-Hut approximation reduces complexity to O(n log n) by treating distant node clusters as single masses.\n\n## Reasoning\nForce layout is the most expensive operation in the app, blocking the main thread for 2-5 seconds on large graphs. This single optimization could reduce layout time by 90%+ for graphs with 500+ nodes. The web worker already exists but processes the same inefficient algorithm.\n\n\n## Recommended Skills\n\nUse Claude Code skills as appropriate for implementation guidance. Check `.claude/skills/` directory for available skills.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n\n## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n\n1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n   - title: 2-6 word summary\n   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n\n2. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n\nBegin implementation now."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d184f0d2-244e-457f-8ea5-4627f2d647f1","uuid":"1c6736e7-7d09-47b8-8992-7dd0fe01831c","isSynthetic":true}
