[2026-02-04T00:23:27.802Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01RjhqhWaXwfzwFsLD8NB6XB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementation complete. Here's a summary:\n\n## Implementation Summary: Barnes-Hut Tree for O(n log n) Force Layout\n\n### Changes Made to `src/lib/graphAlgorithms.ts`\n\n**1. Added Barnes-Hut Quadtree Implementation (lines 708-943):**\n\n- `QuadTreeNode` interface - represents a cell in the spatial partitioning tree containing:\n  - Bounds (x, y, width, height)\n  - Center of mass (cx, cy)\n  - Total mass (number of nodes in subtree)\n  - Children array (NW, NE, SW, SE) for internal nodes\n  - Body reference for leaf nodes\n\n- `BarnesHutTree` class with:\n  - `build(nodes)` - constructs the quadtree from node positions in O(n log n)\n  - `insert(node, body)` - inserts a body into the tree, subdividing as needed\n  - `computeMass(node)` - bottom-up computation of centers of mass\n  - `calculateForce(px, py, nodeIndex, repulsion, alpha)` - computes repulsion force using the approximation\n\n**2. Updated `forceLayout` function (lines 987-1017):**\n\n- Creates a `BarnesHutTree` instance with θ=0.5 (good accuracy/speed balance)\n- Rebuilds the tree each iteration with current node positions\n- Replaced the nested O(n²) loop with O(n) calls to `calculateForce`, each of which is O(log n)\n\n### Algorithm Details\n\nThe Barnes-Hut algorithm works by:\n1. Spatially partitioning all nodes into a quadtree\n2. For each node, traversing the tree and deciding whether to:\n   - Use a cell's center of mass as an approximation (when `s/d < θ`, where s=cell size, d=distance)\n   - Recurse into children for more accuracy (when close to the cell)\n\n### Performance Impact\n\n- **Before**: O(n²) per iteration → For 500 nodes × 100 iterations = 25M force calculations\n- **After**: O(n log n) per iteration → For 500 nodes × 100 iterations ≈ 450K calculations (log₂500 ≈ 9)\n- **Expected speedup**: 50-100x for graphs with 500+ nodes, reducing layout time from 2-5 seconds to ~50-100ms"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":233,"cache_read_input_tokens":101155,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":233},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d184f0d2-244e-457f-8ea5-4627f2d647f1","uuid":"ce916807-129c-4667-af2c-ba67b6db60c6"}
